    "bullets": [
      "Added level gating to the dread V1 evolution menu in Old Dreadnoughts, so level 45 gives tier 1 `dreadOfficialV1` and the tier 2 body choice, level 80 opens the tier 3 body plus body combo, and level 120 opens the tier 4 weapon plus weapon final form.",
      "Changed the evolution menu to pop the moment the player crosses a threshold, in any area, whether that is the forge, the labyrinth or the main arena.",
      "Changed Don't Upgrade to permanently suppress future dread auto popups for the rest of the run, including the class tree open and close bypass path that used to slip past it.",
      "Scoped the gating to the `old-dreadnoughts` mode and a tank tree root of `dreadOfficialV1`, so in every other mode the existing debug menu's dreads addon still shows every tier immediately.",
      "Put the gate levels in a new `DREAD_V1_GATE_LEVELS` map in `game/evolutionTree.ts` instead of mutating `entry.tier`, since mutating the tier would have ballooned `ClassTreeView` vertical spacing 45 times over and broken the tier label formula.",
      "Added a `GameState.dreadUpgradeDismissed` flag, the gate check with its helper and dismiss method, four visibility flip sites, the test mode entry and exit resets, and routed Don't Upgrade through `dismissEvolutionMenu()`.",
      "Fixed the new tier gating blocking the developer tank menu's chain from `menu_addons` to `dreadOfficialV1` to bodies to combos to final weapon forms, since `_computeEvolutions` filters by player level for any dread tank in Old Dreadnoughts.",
      "Added `state.devMenuBypassActive`, scoped to the case where the user is currently navigating the P menu chain, so while it is set `_computeEvolutions` skips the level gate for dread tanks.",
      "Changed the P key handler to set the bypass flag and also clear any prior dread dismissal lock, so the menu can show fresh.",
      "Changed the bypass flag to clear on `enterTestMode` and `exitTestMode`, on `dismissEvolutionMenu`, and at the end of `evolveToTank`, so leaving the dread and menu trees entirely or reaching a leaf clears it immediately.",
      "Verified the bypass is truly scoped three ways, since debug mode alone does not bypass gating, forge reentry and natural level ups gate normally again after the chain ends, and outside Old Dreadnoughts the gate block is skipped entirely.",
      "Fixed the Old Dreadnoughts labyrinth being locked to 128 by 128, since the iconic pattern behind `run8TeamsLabyrinth` is a hand drawn ASCII map of exactly 128 rows by 128 columns, producing a world of 19,200 units per axis at a map scale of 5.",
      "Fixed the 32 and 64 buttons in `MapDesignerUI` being greyed out, since the `MAZE_NATIVE_GRID` entry at key 80 was 128, which force promoted any smaller request back up.",
      "Added `runCompactLabyrinth`, a procedural compact labyrinth generator mirroring the canonical five zone macrostructure at any grid size, with a border inset of about 6.25%, a corner size of about 12.5% and a centre half of about 12.5%.",
      "Added one cell connecting corridors through the middle row and column to guarantee connectivity before erosion runs.",
      "Decoupled cell size in world units from the grid count, staying at the map scale times 30, which is 150 by default, so corridors after erosion stay 150 units wide whichever size is picked.",
      "Preserved the fine tuned tank growth tuning that ensures maximum size tanks and dreads can always squeeze through, since the world shrinks by having fewer cells rather than narrower ones.",
      "Added three sizes: 128 by 128 at 19,200 units per axis using the canonical pattern, 64 by 64 at 9,600 units per axis which is the new Old Dreadnoughts default, and 32 by 32 at 4,800 units per axis.",
      "Changed the `run8TeamsLabyrinth` entry point to dispatch by size, using the canonical hand drawn pattern at exactly 128 and the procedural one at 32 and 64.",
      "Scaled erosion iteration counts by area ratio, from 1,019 operations at 128 squared down to about 64 at 32 squared, so maze density stays consistent across sizes.",
      "Dropped the `MAZE_NATIVE_GRID` entry at key 80 from 128 to 32, the new minimum, which ungreys the 32 and 64 buttons in `MapDesignerUI` with no UI code changes at all.",
      "Moved the Old Dreadnoughts maze area config from `gridCells` 32, which auto promoted to 128, to `gridCells` 64, the new recommended default, with any of the three sizes still pickable from the Map Designer.",
      "Added a `_requestedGridCells` field on the generator and a `_carveRect` helper for carving open regions, roughly 80 lines in all.",
      "Kept the centre reachability safety check `_ensureLabyrinthCenterReachable` at 128 only by design, since the procedural pattern's explicit corridor seeding already guarantees connectivity at the smaller sizes.",
      "Fixed 14 TypeScript errors across 7 files with zero runtime impact: `ClassTreeView` and `TankEvolutionMenu` now use a named import for `GameLogic`, `useBackdropClose` imports the React namespace it needs, and three unused `ts-expect-error` directives were dropped.",
      "Changed menu tank `statNamesType` from default to `generic` in `evolutionTree`, matching the fallback used everywhere else in the codebase.",
      "Changed `createEmptyEnemy` to initialise six `EnemyTank` fields it had been leaving out: `invisEnabled`, `FadeIn`, `FadeOut`, `Alpha` set to 1, `lastFireFrame` set to 0 and `displayName` set to an empty string.",
      "Fixed the debug overlay reading `enemy.configName`, a field that never existed, so it logged blank names; it now reads `enemy.displayName`.",
      "Fixed the test harness diagnostic referencing `tankMaxHealth` and `tankMaxShield`, which do not exist and had been writing NaN into the harness log file, so both are now computed properly.",
      "Fixed the wall edit highlight in `GameCanvas` using `currentZoom` before defining it, a dormant `ReferenceError` waiting to fire, so it now defines the value locally first.",
      "Changed the test harness `facingType` from `toAim` to `faceTarget`, which is snap aim and therefore deterministic.",
      "Fixed a sub turret bullet identifier bug, since `SubTurretConfig` has no `id` field so the old assignment of `child.sourceTurretId` always produced an empty string and per sub turret bullet caps never worked.",
      "Changed it to take the sub turret's own `turretData` id, falling back to the parent's `sourceTurretId` and then to an empty string.",
      "Followed a master and source model for that identifier chain, where `ownerId` is the root tank and `sourceTurretId` is the immediate firing gun, handling infinite nesting because each child either uses its own turret id or inherits the parent's chain."
    ]
