      "Separated the row actions so they are spatially distinct: the chevron on the left expands and collapses the assigned tank list, the name enters inline rename, and the three icons on the right add tanks, configure and delete.",
      "Added a subtle hover state on the name, a background fill plus accent text color, so it reads as interactive without having to hover and wait for the title tooltip.",
      "Changed the rename field to auto select its existing text on focus, so a new name can be typed without clearing the old one first.",
      "Fixed ram mode so rammers actually body ram, since setting distance from target to 0 already wrote `preferredDistance = 0` and `minAttackDistance = 0` but `updateEnemyAttacking` still worked out a soft minimum of 50 and a maximum of 100.",
      "Changed both `softMinDist` and `maxDist` to collapse to 0 when the ram marker is present at spawn, which makes the distance test inside `calculateCombatHoldDirectionInto` always true and puts the tank on the chase branch every frame.",
      "Removed the disengage impulse from ram mode, since with `maxDist` at 0 it can never fire, while the rush impulse still fires normally at its 5 to 10% chance.",
      "Changed the Configure popup aimbot strength default from 50 to 25, matching what spawn and the enemy config popup already use.",
      "Remapped the distance slider so 50 lands at roughly 350 world units instead of roughly 474, with a piecewise curve: 5 or below gives 0, 6 to 50 spans 180 to 350, and 50 to 100 spans 350 to 700.",
      "Changed the distance label under the slider to read Ram mode (charge straight in, no orbit) rather than the old (no minimum).",
      "Left the remaining Configure popup defaults alone, since always shoot off, keep attacking through cover off and flee threshold 0 already matched the engine.",
      "Fixed the retreat trigger forcing a retreat whenever distance dropped below 220, so a smasher charged in, hit the threshold, retreated for about 600 milliseconds, closed again and retreated again, showing up as left and right jitter.",
      "Fixed the combat hold pipeline as the second cause, since it added bias angles from `personality.currentMovementBias`, then `snapDirectionTo8Way` snapped the result to one of eight cardinal directions, then a lerp smoothed it over roughly 150 milliseconds.",
      "Changed ram mode to skip both blocks and write `combatTargetDirX/Y` and `combatHeldDirX/Y` straight to the toward target unit vector every frame, so the smoothing lerp becomes a no op and wall validation still runs.",
      "Changed the result so rammers charge directly at the player every frame, follow when the player tries to back away, and only deflect off walls, with no orbit, no retreat, no jitter and no eight way snap.",
