      "Built a dedicated Skill Upgrade Priorities popup with a banner explaining that the number is priority order and not points to spend, a Skill, Enabled and Priority column strip, per skill rows with a colored dot, toggle and numeric input clamped to 1 to 99, and a z index of 70.",
      "Placed the Custom Upgrade Logic toggle below the Flee HP Threshold behind a divider, revealing a Configure Skills button with a small badge counting how many skills are enabled.",
      "Audited the edge cases: pooled enemies, an empty category, every listed skill maxed with fill randomly off or on, tied priorities round robining with no drift, and editing a category while a categorized enemy is alive.",
      "Fixed the per skill toggles in the Skill Upgrade Priorities popup rendering as static grey circles instead of working switches.",
      "Fixed the root cause of the broken per skill toggles, the markup being wrapped in a label element, since the `toggle-ios` rule sets a 36 by 20 pixel box but a label is display inline by default so the explicit width and height were ignored.",
      "Switched to the div wrapper that every other working toggle in the project uses, inside a flex row so the toggle lines up vertically with the label and the priority input.",
      "Fixed a race where custom upgrade logic was skipped entirely for a tank's initial skill points, since every tank starts with its bonus skill points, 42 by default, plus its base level points, and the spawn time upgrade loop spent all of them before the category override had run.",
      "Fixed why it looked like it only worked sometimes, since those first 42 points went through the default Offensive Weighted logic while points earned from XP later in the match did use the custom priorities.",
      "Split the category override into two halves and moved the non personality half ahead of the upgrade loop, leaving the late half to set only preferred distance and orbit distance, which need the movement personality to exist first.",
      "Changed pooled enemies to have their optional fields cleared before the upgrade loop rather than before the late block, so a recycled slot cannot carry stale priorities into the next spawn's upgrade loop.",
      "Made the category the single source of truth in the interface, so when a tank belongs to a category the matching fields in the Add and Edit Enemy popup become read only mirrors.",
      "Renamed the always shoot setting and its label to Force Autoshoot to match the engine field name, added a Force Autospin toggle below it with a description, and made spawn override `enemy.forceAutospin` from the category too.",
      "Locked four fields: the Upgrade Logic dropdown showing a single option of either Custom Upgrade Logic or Random, the Aimbot Strength slider showing the category's value, and the Force Autoshoot and Force Autospin toggles mirroring the category.",
      "Changed spawn to force the tank's upgrade logic to Random when custom upgrade logic is enabled but no skills are switched on, so the locked dropdown reading Random matches what actually runs.",
      "Scoped the lock rather than making it blanket, so a tank in a category whose Custom Upgrade Logic toggle is off keeps a fully editable Upgrade Logic dropdown while its other fields stay locked.",
      "Added a lock icon beside each locked field's label and helper text naming the owning category in the accent colour, with locked toggle rows dropping to 60% opacity and pointer events left on for the lock icon.",
      "Changed the lock lookup to use `sourceLibraryName` first, then the enemy name, then the library item name, the same key the engine uses at spawn, so renaming an enemy cannot be used to slip out of the lock.",
      "Changed `handleSave()` to write the category's values for the locked fields rather than local state, so the saved enemy config record stays consistent with whatever the category currently holds.",
      "Changed tied priorities from a deterministic round robin to a uniform random pick among the unmaxed skills in the active tier, so two tanks in the same category end up with meaningfully different splits.",
