      "Left snap off, circles and any case where the fit never fires collapsing to identity, so existing placements are exactly backward compatible, with auto pieces inside a preset excluded for Horus parity.",
      "Interlocked compass and snap on polygon bodies of three or more sides, so turning compass on also turns snap on and turning snap off also turns compass off, while on circles the two stay independent.",
      "Batched both handlers into a single `updateState` call so React rerenders once instead of twice, composing with the snap auto sync without any chance of a loop.",
      "Made the library preset width to flat side ratio constant across every polygon layer, since the aspect ratio fix only ran when the width fit fired so a preset that did not overflow simply drifted upward.",
      "Measured Barricade at about 80% of the flat side on the 5 sided main body, about 116% on a 7 sided layer and about 142% on an 8 sided layer, with the fit then clamping both down to 90%.",
