      "Composed the two bakes cleanly, so a same shape layer collapses to the pure `kWidth` bake, a preset with no fit collapses to the pure `sideCorr` bake, and both at 1 is the identity.",
      "Accepted a trade off, that drones and other projectiles spawned from library presets on multi layer bosses are now smaller on more sided layers, because projectile size follows barrel width.",
      "Fixed the compass count not resyncing to the active layer's side count on every transition, since adding a body layer switches to it automatically and a new layer defaults to two more sides, but `state.autoPlacementCount` was never updated.",
      "Added an effect in `TurretManagerUI.tsx` that watches `activeSides` and writes `state.autoPlacementCount` on every transition, using the side count on polygons and 8 on circles, deliberately not depending on `autoPlacementCount` so a manual slider adjustment sticks.",
      "Took a first pass at making barrels fully visible on body layers, after testing showed visibility falling away as side count rose: 100% on layer 1 with 3 sides, 70 to 80% on layer 2, 40 to 50% on layer 3, and 5 to 10% by layer 5.",
      "Fixed the root cause, that the earlier shift was built to preserve the fraction of barrel visible on the main body, which is typically 20 to 50%, so preserving a low fraction on every layer is exactly the falling visibility reported.",
      "Replaced it with adding the layer's `apothemFrac` outright, which for a piece at `xOffset` 0 puts the barrel base at the apothem and leaves the whole barrel showing, applied at four sites.",
      "Recorded the known trade offs of that version: the visible fraction relative to the main body was no longer preserved, multi piece presets stuck out farther, and a same shape body layer now picked up a shift where it previously had none.",
      "Reverted that visibility shift after testing, since the apothem only shift made barrels look two to three times longer than intended, delivering about a 200% increase where the goal was about 20%.",
