      "Recorded the working hypothesis at that point, that Canvas 2D low alpha thin stroke antialiasing is unreliable on Mali G72 with GaneshGL and the Chromium `msaa_is_slow` workaround, a workaround itself flagged as producing rendering artifacts on that exact GPU.",
      "Added a KeyG handler in `handleInput`, gated on the diagnostic HUD, cycling the grid stroke `globalAlpha` through 0.04, 0.15, 0.30 and 1.0 so the tester could screenshot each level, with step 0 the production default so anyone who never pressed G saw no change.",
      "Added a module level `_GRID_ALPHA_STEPS` constant, a `_diagnosticGridAlphaStep` field and a HUD line reading `gridAlpha=X step=N/3 (KeyG cycles)`, with zero allocations and zero GL changes.",
      "Measured that the alpha stepping ruled out low alpha antialiasing quantization as well, leaving the real cause as Mali's tile based deferred renderer dropping primitives from complex Canvas 2D `stroke()` paths when a single draw call overflows its per tile primitive budget.",
      "Moved grid rendering onto the WebGL geometry pipeline, which already draws 200 or more wall rects per frame on the same hardware without trouble, bypassing the broken Canvas 2D stroke rasterizer entirely.",
      "Removed the cascade failure on that GPU with the same move, since broken tile state was leaking out of the stroke pass into the following `drawImage` composites, the likely cause of the bullets and shapes reported disappearing in the same regions.",
      "Added a new Pass 0 in `GameCanvas.tsx` that renders grid lines as WebGL geometry instances, one push per line, gated on `_wglUnifiedPassActive` and executed before every entity pass so the grid composites underneath tanks, bullets, shapes and walls.",
      "Added a new `rect_fill` batch in `WebGLRenderer.ts`: a fill only centred unit rect of 6 vertices, with no stroke geometry and no rounded corners.",
      "Added that batch so a 1 world unit grid line renders as a clean 1 unit line instead of the wall style 7 unit band, which is 1 fill plus 3 strokes on each side plus arcs.",
      "Added a `setSampleAlphaToCoverage(enabled)` method to `WebGLRenderer` and switched it off around the grid flush, so the 0.04 alpha grid is not quantized down to 0 MSAA samples and made invisible, switching it back on immediately afterwards.",
      "Kept the Canvas 2D grid stroke path for the map designer only, gated on `!logic.state.isTestMode`, since the map designer runs outside the WebGL unified pass and never reproduced the fault.",
