      "Closed the diagonal leak in ray casting, so rays now check the L shaped intermediate cells on diagonal grid transitions and enemies can no longer target through the corner gap where two walls meet.",
      "Simplified maze exploration from a three mode forward bias system down to two modes, a 50% forward commit and a 50% random explore with backward rays excluded, removing the perpendicular reversal hack.",
      "Changed enemy speed to be correctly divided by zoom in every state, so it matches player physics.",
      "Added the Direction Hold System, where an enemy commits to a movement direction for 300 to 800ms the way a player holds a key, removing the per frame jitter and the mirror movement that came with it.",
      "Changed the orbit tangent to an absolute world direction, which breaks the mirror effect where an orbiting enemy tracked the player own movement.",
      "Added distance zone retreat, so an enemy backs away once the player closes inside 220 units and commits to that retreat for 400 to 900ms.",
      "Added a following state, so when line of sight breaks the enemy navigates toward the player through the flow field instead of instantly forgetting them, with no obstacle avoidance blend applied because the flow field already handles walls.",
      "Throttled the line of sight checks in the following state, which stops the attacking and following states flickering back and forth.",
      "Changed each enemy movement personality to feed `holdCommitment` and aggressiveness into how long a direction hold lasts and how persistently it keeps following.",
      "Removed the per frame avoidance blend from the attacking state, so attacking now behaves the same way as roaming and following.",
      "Added `validateCombatDirectionWalls()`, a one shot wall check taken at hold time, with a flow field flee fallback so an enemy backed into a corner can still get out.",
